This repository holds a course: its lessons, texts, illustrations, drawings,
mind maps, code examples, tests and quests, together with the software that
publishes them — the site, its components and its build tools.

The course is the author's work. Both the content and the code are covered
by this notice. Nothing here is placed in the public domain, and no licence
to reuse is granted beyond what is written below.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. What you may do without asking
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Read, study and use the course for learning — at js-lessons.pp.ua, at
    garevna.github.io/js-lessons, or from a copy of this repository.
  * Run it locally, and change your own copy while you study it.
  * Quote a short fragment — a paragraph, an example — in a review, a
    lesson of your own, a post or a discussion, naming the author and
    linking to the source.
  * Link to any page of the course.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 2. What needs the author's written permission
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Publishing the course, a lesson, or a substantial part of either —
    anywhere, in any form, including a mirror, a repository of your own, a
    file archive, a video or a printed copy.
  * Translating it into another language and publishing the translation.
  * Making a derivative course, or any other derivative work.
  * Teaching from it for payment, or using it in a paid course, a training
    programme or any commercial offering.
  * Selling it, or including it in anything sold.
  * Using the content to train or fine-tune a machine learning model, or
    including it in a dataset built for that purpose.
  * Removing or altering the copyright notices, in the files or on the page.

Permission is given by the author in writing, and only by the author.
Ask: https://js-lessons.pp.ua (the AUTHOR button), or Telegram @garevna.

